WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/data-display/PollingEngine.tsx — the `PollingEnginePanel` (Adaptive Polling Engine card)
  built on the two polling queries (`getPollingStatus` @ 15s, `getPollingSavings` @ 30s):

    Gate            : `if (!status?.enabled) return null` — the WHOLE surface is withdrawn while the engine is
                      disabled (or the status query has not resolved). No DOM mounts until enabled.
    Header          : TrendingDown glyph + "Adaptive Polling Engine" + an "Active" badge.
    SavingsCard     : when `savings` present — a 4-up metric grid
                        [ savings_percent (1dp) + "%"  (emerald),
                          "$" + estimated_savings (2dp) (emerald),
                          polls_made (int),
                          "$" + remaining_credit (2dp) ]
                      then, when `total = Σ savings_breakdown > 0`, a stacked bar of the positive slices
                      (fleet_telemetry blue / idle_detection amber / prediction purple / sleep_detection gray;
                      width = value/total) + a legend listing all four categories.
    VehicleActivity : for each vehicle — a tap-to-expand row: activity glyph (scale-pulsing ONLY when
                      activity==='active'), vin.slice(-8) (mono), "{activity} · {profileLabel(profile)}" chip,
                      "Next: {formatTimeUntil(next_poll_after)}", a disclosure chevron. Expanded (only when
                      last_decision present): "Interval: {formatDuration(next_interval_ms)}",
                      "Consecutive idle: {consec_idle}", "Battery: {battery_level}%", each reason as "→ {r}",
                      and an optional prediction: "📊 Prediction: {next_state} in
                      {formatDuration(estimated_in / 1e6)} ({round(confidence*100)}% conf)" + "Based on:
                      {based_on}".
    Empty           : enabled but `vehicles.length === 0` → "No vehicles tracked yet. Polling engine will
                      activate on first poll."
  Helpers (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
    formatDuration(ms)   = ms<=0 ? "now" : floor(ms/1000)<60 ? "{s}s" : floor(s/60)<60 ? "{m}m"
                             : "{h}h {m%60}m"   (bare template-literal numbers — NO grouping).
    formatTimeUntil(iso) = diff = parse(iso)-now ; diff<=0 ? "now" : formatDuration(diff).
    activityColor/icon   = active|critical → green/bolt · moderate → blue/battery · low → amber/waveform ·
                             idle → gray/moon · sleeping → slate/moon · default → gray/gauge.
    profileLabel         = driving/charging/idle/sleeping → Title-case; else the raw profile.
    fmtNumber(v,d)       = safeNumber(v).toLocaleString(locale,{min/maxFractionDigits:d}) ; AnimatedNumber
                             renders fmtNumber(value, decimals).
  i18n  : the web source calls t() only in SavingsCard — the eight `polling.*` keys
          (pollsSaved / savedAmount / pollsMade / creditLeft / fleetTelemetry / idleDetection / prediction /
          sleep). Every other string is a hardcoded English literal; per the native no-English-literals rule
          each is promoted to a `pollingEngine.*` key (table "PollingEngine"). The eight web keys are kept
          VERBATIM so "every i18n key from source has a matching key" is literally satisfied.

